<%# THE RUN LIST'S EMPTY STATE — one definition, rendered by BOTH views (the
    table and the cards), so the two can never disagree about why the page is
    empty.

    Two different states, and the page must not confuse them (#10):

      * an empty RESULT SET — a run-state filter is in force and nothing
        matches. "no records match. clear the filters." plus the reset link,
        because the operator's next move is to undo the filter, not to run a
        job.
      * an empty PROJECT — no filter, no runs yet. That is a workspace to
        fill, and the sentence says so. %>
<div class="card empty-state">
  <% if @state.present? %>
    <p>no records match. clear the filters.</p>
    <p class="empty-state-reset">
      no run in this project is <span class="mono"><%= @state %></span> &mdash;
      <%= link_to "Show every run", project_path(@project), class: "query-clear" %>
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p>No runs in this project yet. Run one to get started.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>
